OL,3,AWoman died of heatstroke climbing Yr
OL,4,AWyddfa, inquest hears
OL,5,
OL,6,FA 35-year-old woman died of heatstroke
OL,7,Fon Wales' highest mountain, an inquest
OL,8,Fhas heard.
OL,10,FSophie Goodyer-Bird, from Birmingham,
OL,11,Fwas climbing Yr Wyddfa - also known as
OL,12,FSnowdon - on 10 July, a few days after
OL,13,Fher birthday.
OL,15,FOn Wednesday, an inquest opening at
OL,16,FCaernarfon Coroners' Court heard
OL,17,FGoodyer-Bird became increasingly tired
OL,18,Fwhile coming down the mountain.
OL,20,FNear the end of the walk, she became
OL,21,Funresponsive, and was confirmed to have
OL,22,Fdied shortly afterwards.
OL,23,APub: 02-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
